think The stuck service had a one-line cure the diagnosis earned: no CoreSimulatorService process existed and simctl waits on it silently forever, while open -a Simulator starts the daemon and everything after is ordinary -- the machine note now sits in the reading for the next hand.
think An iPhone 17 Pro booted headless and simctl spawn ran both binaries: the event ring witness answers GREEN with every Swift-born refusal standing inside iOS -- full refuses whole, the counter refuses at the u64 ceiling, order survives the wrap, the aliases one type -- and the parity witness answers lit=16268 with the identical Keccak digest, hex for hex, that the macOS window answered live.
obs Movement four's parity claim now holds across two operating systems from one pinned oracle, with only the compositor-attached Wayland half waiting at the pier; movement five's projection closed with its falsifier never firing. One clock correction rode in honestly: the addendum's first stamp was written from memory while the simulator warmed and the wall clock had walked to morning -- it now carries the stamp the clock actually read, and the lesson is the one-clock law's own.
